// A decision function for the question that comes up constantly.
//
// "The model gets our product details wrong. Should we fine-tune it?"
//
// Almost always: no.
//
//   Symptom                                  Correct intervention
//   ---------------------------------------  ---------------------------
//   Wrong facts about your domain            Retrieval (RAG)
//   Facts change weekly                      Retrieval (RAG)
//   Needs to cite sources                    Retrieval (RAG)
//   Wrong tone or house style                Prompting, then fine-tuning
//   Wrong output format                      Structured output / JSON schema
//   Too verbose                              Prompting
//   Consistent domain-specific behaviour     Fine-tuning
//   Latency or cost too high at volume       Smaller model + fine-tuning
//
// Fine-tuning teaches BEHAVIOUR. Retrieval supplies FACTS.
// Conflating the two is the most expensive mistake in enterprise AI projects:
// months of data preparation to produce a model that is confidently wrong in a
// new way, and stale within a quarter.

